    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "meaning",
      "text": "How do I undo changes if something fails midway in a transaction?",
      "pages": [
        13
      ],
      "answer": "Use the **ROLLBACK** command to undo all changes made in the current transaction when an error occurs. ROLLBACK reverts the database to the state it had before the transaction began, ensuring consistency [1].  \n\nIf you need to keep some earlier work while discarding only the part that failed, create a **SAVEPOINT** before the risky statements and, on error, issue **ROLLBACK TO savepoint_name**; the changes after the savepoint are undone while earlier updates remain [2].",
