    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "meaning",
      "text": "How do I list each employee with their manager's name?",
      "pages": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "answer": "Use a self‑join on the Employees table, joining the employee rows to the manager rows via the ManagerID and EmployeeID columns. For example:\n\n```sql\nSELECT e1.EmployeeName AS Employee,\n       e2.EmployeeName AS Manager\nFROM Employees AS e1\nJOIN Employees AS e2\n     ON e1.ManagerID = e2.EmployeeID;\n```\n\nThis query treats the table as two separate instances (e1 and e2) and returns each employee together with the name of their manager [2].",
